For integration with the hospital information system (SIH) and electronic patient record (DPI), our architecture and integration capabilities include standard connectors and custom adapters. We support health interoperability standards such as HL7 and FHIR through our fhir_hl7_connector. Our API design is API-first, and we can embed our solution in existing work environments.

To ensure data protection, we guarantee strict compliance with the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR). Our hosting infrastructure, operated by OuraneCloud, holds French Hébergeur de Données de Santé (HDS) certification and is SecNumCloud-qualified. We utilize TLS 1.3 for data in transit and AES-256 for data at rest, ensuring the protection of sensitive health data.

Our solution will be deployed on a sovereign HDS tier provided by OuraneCloud, which is EU-only and meets the authority's requirements for data sovereignty. We will provide change management support and staff training to ensure a smooth transition.

In terms of budget, our total contract value is estimated at €900,000 over 5 years, with an annual operating cost compatible with the authority's budgetary capacity. Our pricing model is based on standard daily rates for different roles, with a target gross margin between 25% and 35%. We propose using more cost-efficient tiers or models for hosting and inference to reduce recurring run costs.

Our solution aligns with the CHRB's sustainable development policy by reducing energy consumption and relying on low-carbon infrastructure. Our green hosting with OuraneCloud in the EU region uses renewable energy, has a power usage effectiveness of 1.2, and reuses heat. We practice digital sobriety through model right-sizing, caching, and batching.

Our bid is enhanced by our commitment to providing a high-quality service while respecting the authority's budgetary constraints. We demonstrate our capacity for innovation by leveraging our LLM stack and RAG capabilities to develop a clinical-administrative support solution that meets the client's requirements for explainable recommendations, access to information, improved written output quality, and reduced processing times.

In conclusion, our consortium proposes a comprehensive AI assistance solution that addresses all aspects of the project while meeting the CHRB's requirements and constraints. Our solution will improve staff efficiency, patient care quality, and contribute to environmental sustainability. We are confident that our proposal meets the evaluation criteria for quality and relevance of the proposed solution, compliance with regulatory requirements, level of security, data sovereignty, quality of integration with the existing SIH/DPI, total cost of the solution, consideration of environmental issues, and capacity for innovation.
